Saigon minus Wha-Tonne by chronometer: 1667.65 s of time = 6.9485 deg
French figures: Wha-Tonne adopted 99.7851 E; Saigon 106.7335 E, 10.7798 N
modern longitudes on the Saigon river front: Ba Son, the old naval arsenal on the river (OpenStreetMap) 106.7085 E; the river-front park at Bach Dang 106.7066 E; the botanical garden 106.7063 E
if the camp was at the memorial at Wa Ko (99.7588 E): the Saigon observatory was at 106.7073 E, -0.3 s of time (-0.1 km) from Ba Son
if the camp was where Tisserand's contact times put it, were the French clock right (99.7317 E): the Saigon observatory was at 106.6802 E, -6.8 s of time (-3.1 km) from Ba Son
the French Saigon longitude is 6.3 s of time east of 106.7071 E, as their Wha-Tonne one is 6.3 s east of the memorial (the same error carried over)
